alse,"sync_to_project":"","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"0a873b0b-6e47-5c44-a5be-1505cd882cc8","relative_path":"ramp_earth_1.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# ramp_earth_1\n\nEarth ramp, 1-step: one column wide, 1 column long (along +Z, climbing toward +Z), rising 4 u (1 terrain step of 11.25 cm).\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y -2..4, z -8..8 units.\n- Texture: 64 x 64, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 4, construction_0 6, construction_33 6, construction_66 4, ruined 14 (8 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- ramp wedge: 16 x 4 x 16 (walkable slope 14.0 degrees), centred at the origin\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `ramp_earth_1_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `ramp_earth_1_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_ramp_earth_1` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n"}